ll,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.024657296278503438,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":37.3,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.04111738500273315,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":56.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.016952135279312497,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":71.2,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.013238900117070785,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":77.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.02325,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":15.5,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"PRA Group, Inc., a financial services company, engages in the purchase, collection, and management of nonperforming loan portfolios in the United States, Europe, the United Kingdom, South America, Canada, and Australia. The company purchases loans from credit originators who have chosen not to pursue, or have been unsuccessful in collecting, the full balance owed. It also purchases loans in situations where the customer is involved in a bankruptcy or similar proceeding; and purchase and provide fee-based services for class action claims recoveries. In addition, the company is involved in core and insolvency nonperforming loans include general purpose and private label credit cards, consumer loans, auto loans, overdrafts and small business loans. The company was formerly known as Portfolio Recovery Associates, Inc. and changed its name to PRA Group, Inc. in October 2014. PRA Group, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Norfolk, Virginia.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Martin  Sjolund | CEO, President & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $460K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 8%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["PRA Group, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $486M market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 9-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $90M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -0.1\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 32% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PRA Group (PRAA) Lags Q3 Earnings and Revenue Estimates","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024867/pra-group-praa-lags-q3-earnings-and-revenue-estimates?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cyseop_template_4-3024867","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793915113.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Analyzing PRA Group (NASDAQ:PRAA) and LendingClub (NYSE:LC)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/02/analyzing-pra-group-nasdaqpraa-and-lendingclub-nyselc.html","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793641492.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"PRA Group Q3 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/pra-group-q3-earnings-call-151446783.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793978086.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.153,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"PRA Group Reports Third Quarter 2026 Results","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https